      "q": "1.\n(a) What do you wear in summer?",
      "a": "wer:\nIn summer, we wear cotton clothes.\n(b) What do you wear in winter?\nAnswer:\nIn winter, we wear sweaters, jackets, and other woollen clothes.\n(c) Which season do you like most? Why?\nAnswer:\nWe like the spring season the most because we enjoy the flowers and butterflies, and we can play with friends.\nLook at the pictures and tell the story in your own words.\nAnswer:\nOnce upon a time, a little girl went outside her house with her colourful umbrella. She was excited to play in the rain and feel the raindrops on her face. Suddenly, a playful bird flew by and took her umbrella! The bird was clever and hung the umbrella on a tree branch. But that’s not all—the bird made a cozy nest on the umbrella and put its babies inside. The girl couldn’t believe her eyes! She watched as the bird and its babies enjoyed the shelter of her umbrella in the rain. It was a magical and funny adventure right in her playground.\nLet us Read\nSummer\nBrinda and her family are visiting Hyderabad. Brinda’s grandparents live there. It is hot in Hyderabad. She is wearing a cotton frock.\nWhat are Brinda’s mother, father, grandfather, grandmother, and brother wearing?\nAnswer:\nBrinda’s mother is wearing a Kurti-Salwar, her father a shirt and pants, her grandfather a dhoti-kurta, her grandmother a saree, and her brother a T-shirt and half pants.\nWinter\nPrithvi has gone to Shimla. It is cold there. What is Prithvi wearing?\nAnswer:\nPrithvi is in Shimla where it’s cold. He’s wearing a jacket, muffler, and a woollen hat. In the picture, people are having fun throwing snowballs at each other.\nMonsoon\nCircle the words you see in the picture.\nAnswer:\nThis is an activity for students.\nLet us do\nA Paper Hat\nLook at the pictures and make a paper hat.\nAnswer:\nThis is an activity for students.\nLet us Sing\nPitter Patter\nI hear thunder,\nI hear thunder,\nOh don’t you?\nPitter patter raindrops,\nI am wet through.\nRain\nRain on the green grass,\nRain on the trees,\nRain on the rooftops,\nAnd rain on me.\nLet us write\nWrite down the words that come to your mind when you say summer, winter or monsoon. A few words have been written for you\nSummer\nAnswer:\nhot, sunny, beach, ice cream, vacation, swimsuit, sunburn, relaxation, pool, sunglasses, sandals.\nWinter\nAnswer:\ncold, snow, frost, chilly, fireplace, coat, scarf, gloves, snowflake, holiday, winter sports, cozy.\nSpring\nAnswer:\nblooming flowers, fresh air, greenery, sunshine, blossoms, renewal, new life, pastel colors, picnics, light jackets, growth.\nMonsoon\nAnswer:\numbrella, raindrops, wet, thunderstorms, puddles, overcast, greenery, freshness, drizzle, raincoat, gloomy, cozy.\nBenefits of"
